 "raw_html": "<body><div class=\"eltdf-post-content\">\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-heading\">\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-image\">\n<img alt=\"people recovering\" class=\"attachment-full size-full wp-post-image\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"1081\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" src=\"https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/people-recovering.jpg\" srcset=\"https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/people-recovering.jpg 1920w, https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/people-recovering-300x169.jpg 300w, https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/people-recovering-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/people-recovering-768x432.jpg 768w, https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/people-recovering-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/people-recovering-600x338.jpg 600w\" width=\"1920\"/> </div>\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-info-date entry-date published updated\" itemprop=\"dateCreated\">\n<a data-wpel-link=\"internal\" href=\"https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/2016/00/\" itemprop=\"url\">\n                November 1, 2016        </a>\n<meta content=\"UserComments: 0\" itemprop=\"interactionCount\"/>\n</div> </div>\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-text\">\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-text-inner\">\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-info-top\">\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-info-category\">\n<a data-wpel-link=\"internal\" href=\"https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/category/addiction-rehab/\" rel=\"category tag\">Addiction Rehab</a></div> </div>\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-text-main\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title eltdf-post-title\" itemprop=\"name\">\n            7 Things People Recovering From An Addiction Wish You Knew    </h1> <p>Recovering from an <a data-wpel-link=\"internal\" href=\"https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/\">addiction</a> is difficult when done alone, even well after treatment. It’s important for people to know what their loved one endures while being addicted. That way, families, friends, and spouses can band together to help the person in recovery stick to their sobriety plan.</p>\n<p>Sadly, there are several myths and misconceptions that surround addiction and keep many who suffer from telling others about what they’re going through. One struggle includes the social stigma that often surrounds addiction. People often hesitate to tell their families and friends for fear of being criticized or abandoned.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\">The best thing people can do for someone in recovery from an addiction is stand by their side during their ongoing journey. Contact <a data-wpel-link=\"internal\" href=\"https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/\">Addiction Rehab Centres Canada</a> today!</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-info-bottom clearfix\">\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-info-bottom-left\">\n</div>\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-info-bottom-right\">\n<div class=\"eltdf-post-info-comments-holder\">\n<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"eltdf-icon-font-elegant icon_comment_alt\"></span> <a class=\"eltdf-post-info-comments\" data-wpel-link=\"internal\" href=\"https://addictionrehabcenters.ca/7-things-people-recovering-from-an-addiction-wish-you-knew/#respond\" itemprop=\"url\">\n\t\t\t0 Comments\t\t</a>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div></body>"
}